Collective variables used in the metadynamics of data/dipeptide.pdb

Molecule: ACE - CYS - NME  (capped dipeptide, single CYS residue,
no waters, no ligands, no modifications).

Force field: AMBER ff14SB (via OpenMM amber/ff14SB.xml);
NoCutoff, no periodic boundaries, HBonds constraints; Reference platform;
T=300.0 K; LangevinMiddleIntegrator; dt=2 fs.

CV 1: phi_CYS  -- backbone phi of the central cysteine.
    1-based ATOM indices: (5, 7, 9, 16)
        atom 5  = C(ACE)  (carbonyl C of cap)
        atom 7  = N(CYS)
        atom 9  = CA(CYS)
        atom 16 = C(CYS)  (carbonyl C of cysteine)
    Formula: dihedral(5,7,9,16) in degrees, periodic in 360 deg.

CV 2: psi_CYS  -- backbone psi of the central cysteine.
    1-based ATOM indices: (7, 9, 16, 18)
        atom 7  = N(CYS)
        atom 9  = CA(CYS)
        atom 16 = C(CYS)
        atom 18 = N(NME)
    Formula: dihedral(7,9,16,18) in degrees, periodic in 360 deg.

Rationale: ACE has no preceding residue for phi; NME's terminal CH3-NH
amide is rotationally frozen at 300 K, so its psi is not a meaningful
conformational degree of freedom. Only the central CYS backbone
torsions are rotatable; (phi, psi) of CYS fully spans the conforma-
tional landscape of the capped dipeptide (analogous to the alanine
dipeptide benchmark).

Periodic range used in outputs: [-180, +180) deg, 72x72 cell-centered
grid (cell width 5.0000 deg, cell centers at:
  -177.500, -172.500, -167.500, -162.500, -157.500, -152.500 ...
  ... 167.500, 172.500, 177.500)

Metadynamics parameters (well-tempered WT-MetaD):
  bias factor gamma = 10.0
  initial hill height h0 = 1.0 kJ/mol
  Gaussian sigma per CV = 10.0 deg = 0.174533 rad
  deposition stride = 1.0 ps (500 steps)
  target simulation time = 30 ns (hard cap 100 ns)
  number of hill depositions expected = ~30000

FES reconstruction: F = -(gamma-1)/gamma * V_bias(s) shifted so the
global minimum is 0 (kJ/mol). The deposition rule is replicated
entirely in NumPy:
    h_n = h0 * exp( V_bias_ext(s_n) / (kB * (gamma-1) * T) )
with V_bias_ext constructed only from the externally accumulated
hill list.  OpenMM's getFreeEnergy(), _totalBias, _selfBias,
getTabulatedFunction and getFunctionParameters are NEVER called.

